                  Both contain lactose, because both include whey concentrate alongside isolate. Ghost adds a digestive enzyme blend with lactase, which may help people with mild lactose sensitivity, though the dose is not disclosed. Ryse does not list enzymes on the labels we read. People with real lactose intolerance should consider a whey isolate, clear whey or plant protein instead.
                </p>
