              <summary><h3>Are Ryse and Ghost protein safe?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Both are mainstream whey powders sold by major retailers and are generally fine for healthy adults at one or two scoops a day. Both contain milk, Ryse lists soy in some flavors, and both use artificial sweeteners. People with kidney disease, allergies, digestive conditions, pregnancy or regular medication should check with a doctor or registered dietitian before using a protein supplement.
